# T-10410: `actor` joins the envelope-owned keys — WHO emitted a record is DERIVED host-side from the
# launch context (`_actor` -> lib/memory.py#resolve_actor), never ASSERTED by the caller. Reserving it
# here reuses the existing refusal (no new guard, P1 F1): a `--data '{"actor":…}'` forgery is rejected
# loudly instead of being silently overwritten by the derive. T-10405's posture, held at this verb too:
# free text never reaches an attribution field.
# T-10735 (X-0603): membership and where-the-value-BELONGS-instead live in ONE structure. A caller who
# reaches for a reserved key has a real need (the boomrocket trial legitimately wanted to record WHICH
# actor an observation came from) — a refusal that only lists the set leaves them guessing, so each
# member carries its sanctioned alternative placement. Both caller-facing surfaces DERIVE from here:
# the `event --data` argparse help (build_parser) and the refusal below. Adding a key here therefore
# reaches --help and the refusal with no second edit; a hand-copied literal in either is the silent
# divergence the suite's differential makes loud (tests/test_t10410_deviation_actor.py probe (5)).
RESERVED_DATA_KEY_REDIRECT = {
    "source":  "envelope-owned (host-stamped at append) — drop it from --data",
    "ts":      "envelope-owned (host-stamped at append) — drop it from --data",
    "type":    "pass the event type POSITIONALLY: `event <type>`",
    "task_id": "pass the id via `--task T-XXXX`",
    # T-11092 (X-0868): `task` is the SIBLING spelling of the key above, and it was the ONE that got
    # written — 217 rows in this repo's journal carry a task binding under `data.task` with BOTH
    # canonical carriers absent (all 217 hand-emitted through THIS verb; there is no code emitter
    # behind any of them). Such a row is invisible to the SPEC-0168 rule-2 resolver every AC-probe
    # class ties by, so its evidence silently falls out of the audit-post packet — and the T-10827
    # excluded-types sink cannot report it either, because that sink's predicate requires the row to
    # tie by task_id in the first place. Reserving it here is the EMITTER half of the fix: it closes
    # the carrier at the single surface all 217 came from, which is what makes the reader-side legacy
    # clause in task._event_task_id a bounded read over a frozen population instead of a third open
    # ingress. No doc, seed or brief teaches the `--data {"task": …}` form (every example already
    # uses `--task`), so nothing taught breaks — only the un-taught habit is refused.
    "task":    "pass the id via `--task T-XXXX` (the envelope carrier readers tie by; a binding "
               "left under data.task is invisible to the audit-post evidence packet — T-11092)",
    "actor":   "host-DERIVED from the launch context (SPEC-0086 rule 1), never caller-asserted — to "
               "record an OBSERVED third party, use a non-reserved key such as `observed_actor`",
}
RESERVED_DATA_KEYS = frozenset(RESERVED_DATA_KEY_REDIRECT)

