# whole purpose is to carry something a later reader can act on. `event` accepts a free-form type and
# an EMPTY `--data` ({} — `if args.data:` skips an empty string), so a capture that carries nothing
# triageable records a well-formed row that is indistinguishable from noise in the fold.
#
# BOUNDED TO THESE THREE deliberately. The ~76 other types this generic verb accepts are lifecycle
# MARKERS whose TYPE is the content (a `graph_built` needs no payload to mean what it means), so
# warning on them would be alarm erosion — the same reason the short-sha near-miss below fires only
# on a DEMONSTRATED near-miss and stays silent on healthy rows. These three are exactly the types
# this verb already reads `data` semantics out of (the `wait_reason` derive two blocks down): a
# capture with no cause, and a halt or a pause with no reason, each leave a reader with a row that
# says only that SOMETHING happened.
